ames `RateSource`; the 'No unused Terraform declarations remain' AC is scoped to `terraform validate`, not the Python module"],"finding":"The removal inventory lists `MeteredRate` for deletion but omits the module-level `RateSource = Literal[\"empirical\", \"seed\", \"empirical_scaled\", \"fallback\"]` alias (handler.py:311), whose only reference is `MeteredRate.source` (handler.py:317). Grep for `RateSource` returns exactly those two lines, so deleting `MeteredRate` leaves `RateSource` as a dead orphan not named anywhere in the plan's inventory or acceptance criteria.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f69a408c83a72bcde","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — \"The seven pricing functions ... and six constants ... are absent\" and \"`state[\"rates\"]`, `state[\"rates_day\"]`, `metered_estimated`, `MeteredRate` ... are removed\"","norm_id":"n325b92070d87cefc","priority":0.385,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["handler.py retains the orphaned `RateSource` Literal alias after `MeteredRate` is deleted, leaving dead code that no test or lint gate in the plan flags","If `Literal` is also dropped from the typing import when MeteredRate goes, a dangling `RateSource` referencing `Literal` would break import"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend the MeteredRate removal AC to also assert `RateSource` is absent, and confirm via find_referencing_symbols that no other consumer of `RateSource` exists before deletion.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_